Joint output ownership:
  cbv-coercion (014): independently produces tuple-arithmetic's pre CBD and an
    explicit64-primops CBD. The owning arithmetic producers must be the sole
    writers; a consumer needing those files must depend on their producers.
  mutable-bytearrays (019), resize-bytearrays (020), mutable-bytearray-size (021),
    array-slices (123): regenerate build/primop-coverage.json from inside recipes.
    Shared coverage must have one separate owning rule.
  backend-annotations (040): independently publishes build/thc-fixtures.path,
    also published by compact-model and common/default setup. The backend fixture
    must consume the encoder from one shared owner instead.
  simd-capability-smoke (116): invokes the generator that also writes application
    Java/fixture sources through Gradle. The generator needs one owner and the
    fixture must consume the generated sources, not regenerate them.

Shared infrastructure also excluded from translation as fixture rules:
  interface-core (085): runs InstalledCacheFixtures.checkInstalledCache during
    generation, destroys/recreates its cache, corrupts interfaces and sources, and
    publishes test-success booleans. A fixture cache hit would skip those tests.
    Package DB initialization also changes the published log set on repeat runs.
    Separate retained/thin interface products and native linkage artifacts from
    cache-correctness tests; run the latter as tests with private scratch state.
    Both pinned-source and complete retained-Core provider paths remain required.

Not quarantined merely for this reason:
  Test-private filesystem state used to check unlink/rename/directory semantics.
  A shared tool called by several rules, provided its products have ONE owning
    rule and callers only consume those products.
  The application runtime's native providers are Gradle-owned application products,
    not fixture admission decisions. Their incrementality defects are recorded in
    fixture-inputs.log's shared appendix and still need repair at their owner.

Compiler-structure assertions (also excluded):
  aligned-scalar-memory (052): exact Core/root/primitive-use expectations.
  original-open (069): exact internal root counts.
  tuple-join (124), sum-join (137): exact join/state-lambda/case shapes; generated
    receipt/audit files are not consumed by their behavioral tests.
  original-time-clock (140, custom full-Core): expects exactly one/two executed
    roots and retains a dedicated time/base CAPI fixture harness. Its consumer
    is listed in quarantinedJunit and excluded by every Gradle Test task.

  rts-event (141, custom full-Core): three recursive producer subprocesses rewrite
    the parent's GHC/log paths; exact compiled-entry counts and a broad native
    eventfd/pipe/poll harness. RtsEventNativeTest is excluded. Its independent
    safe-completion masking test should move to fixture-free runtime coverage.

  gc-stats (142, custom full-Core): requires native RTS stats disabled without
    declaring/configuring the producer RTS environment; exact compiled-entry
    counts and twelve audits for trivial reference observations. GcStatsNativeTest
    is excluded. Preserve the useful no-write buffer guard in focused coverage.

  aggregate-heap (145, custom full-Core): both producer and consumer enumerate
    stage/Core output directories. AggregateHeapNativeTest is excluded until named
    module outputs replace the hidden input set. Preserve useful heap layout and
    laziness behavior when consolidating aggregate tests.

  fourway-aggregate (146, custom full-Core): producer and native consumer discover
    stage CBDs by listing output directories. All three FourWayAggregate native,
    storage and protocol consumer classes are excluded until ownership is fixed.

  narrow-integer-transport (147, custom full-Core): both sides list stage CBDs.
    NarrowIntegerTransportTest is excluded. After repair this general corpus may
    replace smaller narrow fixtures; split SIMD so scalar coverage does not force LLVM.

  generic-sum-transport (148, custom full-Core): producer and consumer list stage
    CBDs. GenericSumTransportTest is excluded. Keep typed carrier/GC-lifetime
    boundaries and recover direct storage/rejection controls without native setup.

  tuple-join-input (149): generation freezes minimum join/case counts and unconditionally requires an
    original-library reference even with that mode disabled. TupleJoinNativeTest
    excluded. Preserve first-compiled/empty-join semantic checks when consolidating.

  sum-input (150): generation freezes sum-formal/capture/partial-application shapes and exact
